{"name":"Ice Floe","hex":"#d8e7e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice floe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any type of sea ice not attached to land, drift ice.","An ice dam (ice jam), a blockage of ice in a river starting with an ice floe in the river."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice_floe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice floe","blocks":[{"text":"An ice floe is a segment of floating ice defined as a flat piece at least 20 metres (66 ft) across at its widest point, and up to more than 10 kilometres across. Drift ice is a floating field of sea ice composed of several ice floes. They may cause ice jams on freshwater rivers, and in the open ocean may damage the hulls of ships."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_floe","wikidata":"Q368930"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Drift_ice_in_Hudson_Strait%2C_2014.jpg/250px-Drift_ice_in_Hudson_Strait%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Drift_ice_in_Hudson_Strait%2C_2014.jpg/500px-Drift_ice_in_Hudson_Strait%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Drift_ice_in_Hudson_Strait%2C_2014.jpg/250px-Drift_ice_in_Hudson_Strait%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADrift_ice_in_Hudson_Strait%2C_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/eb/IceNomenclature-2LightPack.jpg/250px-IceNomenclature-2LightPack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/IceNomenclature-2LightPack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/eb/IceNomenclature-2LightPack.jpg/250px-IceNomenclature-2LightPack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIceNomenclature-2LightPack.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/In_the_Arctic_Sea_-_An_Ice_Floe_Adrift_%28NBY_439626%29.jpg/250px-In_the_Arctic_Sea_-_An_Ice_Floe_Adrift_%28NBY_439626%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/In_the_Arctic_Sea_-_An_Ice_Floe_Adrift_%28NBY_439626%29.jpg/500px-In_the_Arctic_Sea_-_An_Ice_Floe_Adrift_%28NBY_439626%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/In_the_Arctic_Sea_-_An_Ice_Floe_Adrift_%28NBY_439626%29.jpg/250px-In_the_Arctic_Sea_-_An_Ice_Floe_Adrift_%28NBY_439626%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIn_the_Arctic_Sea_-_An_Ice_Floe_Adrift_(NBY_439626).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi